{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790996321,"nonce":"ffWYlsrw/TmVYJ44xtiJL5F6y+s=","message":"Fixed in fc5c3ab7af427653acdee6021f2d7b77921d48a0. Not the GC and not a Cranelift miscompile. Interaction.setDisabled(true) reaches SignalBool.set through ISignal\u003cBool\u003e (HVIRTUAL, erased T), so the Bool arrives boxed. execute_function unboxes args against the callee's declared kinds before an interpreted body (coerce_value_for_static_kind), but call_compiled_entry only boxed for Dynamic params and forwarded everything else, so compiled SignalBool.set (findex 341) received the box's address; its low byte is 0 on an aligned pointer, so set(true) passed 0. Found by tracing set_bool/get_bool in an instrumented copy of blinc_abi: the first interp/hybrid divergence was set_bool(H36, 1) vs set_bool(H36, 0). Handle and finalizer instrumentation showed no emptied or foreign handles. Hybrid-only because it needs an interpreted caller and a compiled callee; 'partway through' is when set gets compiled. Regression: crates/ash_cli/tests/boxed_primitive_arg.rs (standalone, no blinc); without the fix it gives 940 wrong of 20000 under hybrid (319 with ASH_OSR=0), jit 0. ashui hybrid_signal/run.sh: ALL PASSED in all three modes, and the 03:20 snapshot of the failing smoke.hl passes 3/3 hybrid. Unit conformance 1069/1069 interp/hybrid/jit; hdll_callbacks no regressions.","files":null}]}